+# QIK-VRT Planck-tick gap law v1
+
+**Author:** Ingolf Lohmann  
+**Status:** falsifiable physical hypothesis; not empirically confirmed  
+**Repository boundary:** exact model and prediction contract in `physics/planck_tick_gap_law_v1.json`
+
+## Why this crosses the formalism-to-physics threshold
+
+The existing QIK-VRT H5 work already separates formal identities, causal/evidence binding and measurement-derived structure from physical correspondence. Its open H5-O05 gate asks for a differentiating numerical prediction with an observable, uncertainty/falsifier, data mapping and independent reproduction.
+
+This note freezes one explicit physical instantiation of the Universal-Terminal tick. It is intentionally stronger than a change of units or coordinates. It changes the phase law of a bound quantum excitation and therefore produces an observable deviation from ordinary continuous-time quantum mechanics.
+
+It does **not** claim empirical confirmation. The threshold crossed here is from a model-theoretic framework to a falsifiable physical hypothesis.
+
+## PTG-P01 — physical postulate
+
+Let a bound quantum system have a self-adjoint Hamiltonian `H` with ground energy `E0`. Define the ground-referenced Hamiltonian
+
+```text
+Hc = H - E0 I
+```
+
+so that an arbitrary additive energy-zero change `H -> H + C I` leaves `Hc` unchanged.
+
+Freeze the Universal-Terminal tick to the Planck time
+
+```text
+tP = sqrt(hbar G / c^5)
+EP = hbar / tP = sqrt(hbar c^5 / G)
+```
+
+and postulate symmetric finite-difference phase evolution
+
+```text
+i hbar [psi(t+tP) - psi(t-tP)] / (2 tP) = Hc psi(t).
+```
+
+For an energy eigenstate with excitation gap
+
+```text
+DeltaE = E - E0,
+```
+
+insert
+
+```text
+psi(t) = exp(-i omega t) psi(0).
+```
+
+Then
+
+```text
+psi(t+tP)-psi(t-tP)
+= -2 i sin(omega tP) psi(t),
+```
+
+and the evolution law becomes
+
+```text
+hbar sin(omega tP)/tP = DeltaE.
+```
+
+Since `EP = hbar/tP`, define `x = DeltaE/EP`. On the low-energy branch `0 <= x < 1`, the exact prediction is
+
+```text
+omega_Q = asin(x)/tP.
+```
+
+Ordinary quantum mechanics predicts
+
+```text
+omega_0 = DeltaE/hbar = x/tP.
+```
+
+Therefore QIK-VRT Planck-tick v1 predicts the exact positive residual
+
+```text
+delta_omega
+= omega_Q - omega_0
+= [asin(x)-x]/tP > 0       for 0 < x < 1.
+```
+
+This cannot be generated by a mere invertible reparameterization while preserving the standard dynamics and observable map: it is a different phase-evolution law.
+
+## Low-energy prediction
+
+Using
+
+```text
+asin(x) = x + x^3/6 + 3 x^5/40 + ...,
+```
+
+we obtain
+
+```text
+delta_omega
+= DeltaE^3 / (6 hbar EP^2)
+  + O(DeltaE^5/EP^4).
+```
+
+The relative deviation is
+
+```text
+omega_Q/omega_0 - 1
+= asin(x)/x - 1
+= x^2/6 + 3 x^4/40 + ... .
+```
+
+There is no adjustable coefficient in v1 once `tP` is fixed by `hbar`, `G` and `c`.
+
+## Frozen numerical examples
+
+Using CODATA-2022 constants as recorded in the machine-readable contract:
+
+| excitation gap | relative shift | `delta_omega` | time for 1 rad excess phase |
+|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 1 eV | `1.1181384583903479e-57` | `1.698751363094503e-42 rad/s` | `5.88667665984012e41 s` |
+| 1 MeV | `1.1181384583903479e-45` | `1.6987513630945025e-24 rad/s` | `5.8866766598401216e23 s` |
+| 1 GeV | `1.1181384583903477e-39` | `1.6987513630945025e-15 rad/s` | `5.886676659840121e14 s` |
+| 1 TeV | `1.1181384583903478e-33` | `1.6987513630945026e-6 rad/s` | `588667.6659840122 s` |
+
+The last row does **not** assert that a presently available coherent two-level platform with a 1 TeV excitation gap can be maintained for roughly 6.81 days. It only freezes the prediction so an experimental-platform search has a precise target.
+
+## Falsifier
+
+For any coherently phase-tracked bound two-level system satisfying the declared domain, determine the excitation gap independently of the phase-fit being tested and measure the residual
+
+```text
+R = omega_measured - DeltaE/hbar.
+```
+
+PTG-P01 predicts
+
+```text
+R = [asin(DeltaE/EP) - DeltaE/EP] / tP > 0.
+```
+
+A validated experimental upper bound
+
+```text
+|R| < delta_omega_QIKVRT
+```
+
+for the same bound system, with uncertainty and systematics below the predicted value, falsifies PTG-P01 in that domain.
+
+Agreement at one gap does not by itself establish the theory; the cubic low-energy scaling
+
+```text
+R proportional to DeltaE^3
+```
+
+must also survive independent tests at distinct gaps.
+
+## Scientific boundary
+
+Finite-difference quantum mechanics and the `chronon` idea are not historically new. Caldirola and later Farias/Recami studied retarded, symmetric and advanced finite-difference formulations decades before QIK-VRT. No priority claim is made for discretizing the Schrödinger equation.
+
+The specific v1 commitment frozen here is narrower and testable:
+
+1. the tick is universal and equals `tP`;
+2. the Hamiltonian is bound to the ground-referenced `Hc`, preserving invariance under an arbitrary additive energy-zero shift;
+3. the symmetric low-energy branch is selected;
+4. the exact gap law is `omega_Q = asin(DeltaE/EP)/tP`;
+5. no free deformation coefficient is admitted in v1.
+
+This turns the QIK-VRT tick from an epistemic/control metaphor into a physical hypothesis with a numerical observable.
+
+## Relation to H5-O05
+
+This artifact closes only the **prediction-freezing** portion of H5-O05. The following remain open and must remain fail-closed:
+
+```text
+experimentally realizable platform
+apparatus and calibration binding
+uncertainty budget below predicted residual
+preregistered data map
+actual measurement
+independent reproduction
+```
+
+Accordingly:
+
+```text
+PHYSICAL_HYPOTHESIS_BOUND = true
+DIFFERENTIATING_PREDICTION_FROZEN = true
+EMPIRICAL_CORRESPONDENCE = false
+INDEPENDENT_REPRODUCTION = false
+PASS = false
+FINAL_PASS = false
+EFFECT_ACK_DONE = false
+```
+
+That is the exact scientific boundary.
